name the handheld on its own sticker

`0007` writes MODEL NO. MIYOO MINI FLIP into the About plate, which was true
when there was one handheld. There are three now -- the Flip, the Mini Plus
and the Mini -- running the same binary off the same card, and two of them
were being told they were something else.

The name comes from the device layer rather than a constant: `Platform` grows
a `model()`, defaulted to upstream's own machine so nothing above the trait
has to know this port exists, and `DevicePlatform` answers it by looking at
what the hardware has.

The same three-way split Allium makes in its boot hook, and the one the
battery already depends on, so it is tested by everything that reads a
charge:

  - a second input node, `/dev/input/event1`, is the Flip's hall sensor;
  - `/customer/app/axp_test` is the Mini Plus's battery tool;
  - `/dev/sar` is what is left, the Mini, whose charge is an ADC (`0022`).

A handheld that answers none of them gets MIYOO rather than a guess. Nothing
reads a model string, because none of these three carries one.

Applies to upstream 91499a9.

